**Correction to the plan's step 4 assumption:** The already-committed `test_delete_two_children_root_triggers_fixup` (the very first whitebox delete test, not one I added this session) actually already exercises the **right/mirror branch** of `delete_fixup` (`src/rbtree.c:256-281`) — specifically the Case 2 mirror. Tracing it: deleting `"d"` leaves `x=NULL` under `x_parent=f`, and since `f->left=b` is non-NULL, the fixup takes the `else` branch (`w = x_parent->left`), not the branch I'd assumed. So a "Case 2 mirror" test would be redundant — the mirror branch isn't actually untested, just Case 1/3/4 mirror specifically are.

Given that, I'm proposing a **Case 4 mirror (direct)** test instead — the mirror image of step 3's tree, reflected left-right:

**Tree (pre-delete):**
```
        r(B)
       /    \
     p(B)   t(B)   <- deleted
     /
   n(R)
```
Keys `n < p < r < t`.

